How to judge:
- Score strictly against the rubric. 10 means a strong staff-level answer, 5 means it
  works but is shallow, 2 means it misses the point of the problem.
- The overall score is your judgement of the design as a whole, not an average.
- Quote or name specifics from the submission. Never give feedback that would apply to
